      "content": "I hear you on the \"learning curve\" part, but it feels like you're still framing the \"discomfort\" as something that just needs to be managed away. Some employees feel like they're being forced to adopt a specific ideological viewpoint through their speech, which they see as a violation of their own values or just plain awkward. Can't we see that as a legitimate, fundamental disagreement rather than just a temporary hurdle to get past?",
